{"name":"Sour Cherry","hex":"#e24736","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sour cherry","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Species of Prunus subg. Cerasus, (cherries), native to much of Europe and southwest Asia, especially, Prunus cerasus, Prunus pseudocerasus, and Prunus cerasoides.","The fruit of these trees, often used for cooking."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour_cherry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prunus cerasus","blocks":[{"text":"Prunus cerasus is an Old World species of Prunus in the subgenus Cerasus (cherries). It has two main groups of cultivars: the dark-red Morello cherry and the lighter-red Amarelle cherry. The sour pulp is edible."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Prunus_cerasus_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-113.jpg/330px-Prunus_cerasus_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-113.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prunus_cerasus"},{"title":"Sourness","blocks":[{"text":"Sourness, also known as sour, is a basic taste sensation perceived through hydrogen ions from acidic compounds interacting with taste bud receptors, and it can also refer to an unpleasant or acidic quality in taste, disposition, or tone. It is a warning sign for potentially spoiled food, though it is balanced in some food products by sweetness, and it is associated with a low pH."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Lemon_with_white_background.jpg/330px-Lemon_with_white_background.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sourness"},{"title":"Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry is the fruit of many plants of the genus Prunus, and is a fleshy drupe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg/330px-Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o